# ELF is required for this one; `run.sh` does it.
#
# This is the survivor, and the measurement is the point. Cycle 8 closed the
# fail-open twice: `emit()` sets the flag from the length it read, AND
# `ferrum_ebpf::path_truncated` derives the same answer from the bytes that
# arrived, so an ELF predating the fix cannot fail open. Measured on this
# kernel with this patch applied: the docker.sock verdict on an over-long path
# is still `kill`, still `path_unknown`, and the probe still dies of SIGKILL.
# The datapath half of the pair is gone and no verdict changes.
